SPARTA (24 Sep 2025)
Running on 4 MPI task(s)
################################################################################
# 3d inflow/outflow flow through a box
#
# Exercises the outflow face on the fast path.  Particles enter at xlo and
# leave through the outflow faces; deleting one that ends the timestep
# outside such a face is done by the optimized move rather than by walking
# the particle to the face cell by cell.  This is the case an inflow/outflow
# problem spends its boundary work on.
#
# Run the same script with "-var opt no" to compare against the normal move.
# On a single processor the two agree exactly, step for step.
#
# Note:
#  - The "comm/sort" option to the "global" command is used to match MPI runs.
#  - The "twopass" option is used to match Kokkos runs.
################################################################################

variable            opt index yes

seed	    	    12345
dimension   	    3
global              gridcut 0.0 comm/sort yes optmove ${opt}
global              gridcut 0.0 comm/sort yes optmove yes

boundary	    o o p

create_box  	    0 0.001 0 0.001 0 0.001
Created orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (0.001 0.001 0.001)
create_grid 	    10 10 10
WARNING: Could not acquire nearby ghost cells b/c grid partition is not clumped (../grid.cpp:483)
Created 1000 child grid cells
  CPU time = 0.00415372 secs
  create/ghost percent = 85.5901 14.4099
balance_grid        rcb part
Balance grid migrated 740 cells
  CPU time = 0.00283497 secs
  reassign/sort/migrate/ghost percent = 44.3391 0.0649038 13.2362 42.3597

species		    ar.species Ar
mixture		    air Ar vstream 300.0 200.0 0.0 temp 300.0

global		    nrho 1.e20 fnum 1.e7

create_particles    air n 0 twopass
Created 9999 particles
  CPU time = 0.00604021 secs
fix                 in emit/face air xlo ylo twopass

fix                 gcheck grid/check 1 error

stats		    100
stats_style	    step cpu np nbound nexit

timestep            2.e-7
run 		    500
